"Implemented (2026-08-12): NARROW STAT TYPES. StatBlock now stamps two int sections: seca_small_int i8 [attack, defense] (play values live in roughly -20..20) and seca_wide_int i16 [mhp, mep] (pools merit 16 bits; user: no valid 32-bit uses for these). Merge saturates (saturating_add) instead of wrapping. Narrowing goes all the way down -- runtime components match rather than widening at the apply boundary: AttackComponent.attack i8; HpComponent hp/mhp/accumulated_damage/accumulated_healing i16, defense i8; EpComponent ep/mep i16; ActionEffect::Attack/Heal payloads i16; StatBlockAsset mirrors (i8/i16). Arithmetic sites widen to i32 for intermediates then clamp back losslessly (hp_system settle, action_system damage = base + attack - defense clamped to [0, i16::MAX]); event accumulation saturates. Unit test added for saturation at type bounds. Future counted-property stats join the i8 section. Gate green: cargo test, clippy 0 errors, bun check (bindings regenerated), 99 unit tests, e2e phases 0-6."